1
00:00:01,040 --> 00:00:02,479
Moses.

2
00:00:02,479 --> 00:00:08,799
They all declared contemptuously that his stories about Sugar Candy Mountain were lies.

3
00:00:08,799 --> 00:00:14,479
And yet, they allowed him to remain on the farm not working with an allowance

4
00:00:14,479 --> 00:00:18,120
of a gill of beer a day.

5
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:22,520
After his hoof had healed up, Boxer worked harder than ever.

6
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:26,639
Indeed, all the animals worked like slaves that year.

7
00:00:26,639 --> 00:00:31,159
Apart from the regular work of the farm and the rebuilding of the windmill,

8
00:00:31,159 --> 00:00:35,799
there was the schoolhouse for the young pigs which was started in March.

9
00:00:35,799 --> 00:00:44,600
Sometimes the long hours on insufficient food were hard to bear. But Boxer never faltered.

10
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:49,840
In nothing that he said or did was there any sign that his strength was not what

11
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:51,399
it had been.

12
00:00:51,399 --> 00:00:54,760
It was only his appearance that was a little altered.

13
00:00:54,760 --> 00:01:00,040
His hide was less shiny than it had used to be and his great haunches seemed to

14
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:01,719
have shrunken.

15
00:01:01,719 --> 00:01:07,479
The others said, >> "Boxer will pick up when the spring grass comes on."

16
00:01:07,479 --> 00:01:12,000
>> But the spring came and Boxer grew no fatter.

17
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,280
Sometimes on the slope leading to the top of the quarry, when he braced his

18
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:21,559
muscles against the weight of some vast boulder, it seemed that nothing kept him

19
00:01:21,559 --> 00:01:25,399
on his feet except the will to continue.

20
00:01:25,399 --> 00:01:32,000
At such times, his lips were seen to form the words, >> "I will work harder."

21
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,159
>> He had no voice left.

22
00:01:35,159 --> 00:01:37,000
Once again, Clover and Benjamin warned
